# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rust / cargo build artefacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/target
target/
**/*.rs.bk
# Release bundles from scripts/build-release.sh.
/dist
# Cargo's normalised manifest left behind by `cargo vendor` / unpacking
# vendored crates. The "real" manifest is the one without `.orig`.
*.orig
*.rej
# More `cargo vendor` artefacts inside the vendored revm-* crates. The
# workspace uses the root Cargo.lock; per-crate lockfiles inside a
# vendored crate are dead weight, and .cargo-ok / .cargo_vcs_info.json
# are extractor markers — none of these are load-bearing.
crates/revm-*/Cargo.lock
crates/revm-*/.cargo-ok
crates/revm-*/.cargo_vcs_info.json
# Coverage / profiling output
*.profraw
*.profdata
tarpaulin-report.*
coverage/
flamegraph.svg
perf.data
perf.data.old

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor / IDE state
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
*.swp
*.swo
*.swn
*~

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI tooling — deliberately NOT in the public repo. Covers per-tool
# state directories AND shared project-instruction files (CLAUDE.md,
# AGENTS.md, .cursorrules, etc.). If you want any of these locally,
# create them after cloning.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude*
CLAUDE.md
.cursor*
AGENTS.md
.aider*
.continue/
.github/copilot-*
.windsurfrules
.codeium/
.tabnine/
.cody/
.openhands/
.openai/
.gemini/
.copilot/
.devin/
.replit/
.zed/
.codex
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS-generated cruft
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets / credentials — defence in depth; nothing should match today.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
secrets/
secrets.*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime data — never commit chain state. Cheap to reproduce, expensive
# (and sometimes consensus-sensitive) to ship.
#
# Paths are anchored to the repo root (leading `/`) so a nested
# `data/` or `db/` test fixture isn't silently swallowed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/mainnet-data/
/testnet-data/
/nile-data/
/shasta-data/
/data/
/db/
/snapshots/
/bench-work/
/sync-test-data/
# Default data_dir from `tron-node init` (config.rs:1072) and the
# scratch dir wired into the integration test harness.
/tron-data/
/test-data/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local logs / debug dumps
#
# Coredump patterns are anchored to root — without the leading `/`,
# a generic `core` rule swallows any directory literally named `core`
# (we have one inside the vendored protos).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
/logs/
/core
/core.*
*.coredump

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Reference repositories cloned for grep / parity work. Not vendored — clone
# them yourself if you want them locally. See README's "Reference
# implementation" section.
#
# Anchored to the repo root so the vendored protos at
# `crates/tron-proto/vendored/java-tron/` are NOT swallowed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/java-tron/
/tronprotocol/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Temporary working directory — scratch notes, in-progress review docs, and
# any other ephemeral artefacts that shouldn't be committed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/working/
